    "streamedUsageUsable": false,
    "finalText": "Everything works now: `node run-tests.js`, the declared check `node checks/contract.cjs` (via the hash-pinned entry in `amabie.project.json` — unchanged), and the new `node checks/deep-contract.cjs` all pass. Committed as `ff85d3b`.\n\n**What was broken and what I changed** (all four defects trace to contract lines 6–9; the API surface is preserved, no checks weakened):\n\n1. **`src/storage.js` — tenant isolation.** `key(tenant, id)` returned just `id`, so the same id in different tenants collided. Now returns `JSON.stringify([tenant, id])`, which decodes back to exactly one pair — collision-free even for delimiter-bearing strings like `a,\"b`/`c` vs `a`/`b\",c`.\n\n2. **`src/replay.js` — replay dropped deletions.** `replay` filtered to `op === 'put'`, so `open(exportJournal())` resurrected deleted pairs. Now applies every event in order, so replayed state (including deletions) matches, and repeated replay stays equivalent.\n\n3. **`src/api.js` `batch` — ignored the event op.** It unconditionally did `rows.set(k, e.value)`, turning a batched `delete` into a stored `undefined` instead of a removal. Batch now routes each event through the existing `mutate`/`apply` path, so ops, ordering, and journal cloning are uniform across put/remove/batch.\n\n4. **`src/api.js` cache — never invalidated.** `get` cached both hits and misses, and no mutation path cleared them, so reads went stale after put/remove/batch. `apply` now deletes the affected key's cache entry, making every read fresh on every mutation path (including after journal replay).\n\n5. **`checks/deep-contract.cjs` (new) — tests** for the clauses the smoke check missed: cross-tenant and delimiter-hostile key independence, cached-hit and cached-miss freshness on all mutation paths, batch delete of absent pairs, exact journal order through batch, replay fidelity across three generations with post-replay mutations, export/input-history detachment, and replayed-miss freshness.\n\nDeliberately untouched: `docs/CONTRACT.md`, `checks/contract.cjs`, `amabie.project.json` — the `proofs` entry binds a hash to the declared check and I couldn't reproduce its format, so I left the declared suite and its proof intact rather than risk invalidating it; the new tests run standalone."
  },
